media: i2c: drivers for the S5KGM1, OV13855 and S5K5E8 sensors

For the sdm660-mainline 7.2.y kernel (tested on v7.2.3-sdm660, Xiaomi Redmi
Note 7 "lavender", Shenchao variant, 4 GB).

Main camera Samsung S5KGM1 (4000x3000, 2000x1500), front camera OmniVision
OV13855 (4224x3136, 2112x1568) and depth camera Samsung S5K5E8 (2592x1944,
1296x972). The three files are generated by scripts/cameras/gen_drivers.py
from a template that follows the structure of s5kjn1.c (Linaro). The
register sequences come from the vendor sensor libraries of MIUI
(libmmcamera_lavender_*.so), which are not part of this repository.

The default frame length is ~10 fps and the minimum is 30 fps: libcamera
0.8 takes the exposure limit from the exposure control at configure time,
so this lets the AGC reach 100 ms in low light and shorten the frame again
when there is light.

Not meant for upstream as is: no DT bindings, and the register tables are
vendor data.

Apply after 0005. Needs the options in kernel-7.2/cameras.config.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
index 5d173e0ec..ba40be8d5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -793,6 +793,36 @@ config VIDEO_S5K6A3
 	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for Samsung S5K6A3 raw
 	  camera sensor.
 
+config VIDEO_S5KGM1
+	tristate "Samsung S5KGM1 sensor support"
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for Samsung S5KGM1 48MP raw
+	  camera sensor.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called s5kgm1.
+
+config VIDEO_S5K5E8
+	tristate "Samsung S5K5E8 sensor support"
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for Samsung S5K5E8 5MP raw
+	  camera sensor.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called s5k5e8.
+
+config VIDEO_OV13855
+	tristate "OmniVision OV13855 sensor support"
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for OmniVision OV13855 13MP raw
+	  camera sensor.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called ov13855.
+
 config VIDEO_S5KJN1
 	tristate "Samsung S5KJN1 sensor support"
 	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
